Presidential elections were held in [[Mongolia]] on 20 May 2001.<ref>[[Dieter Nohlen]], Florian Grotz & Christof Hartmann (2001) ''Elections in Asia: A data handbook, Volume II'', p490 {{ISBN|0-19-924959-8}}</ref> The result was a victory for incumbent [[Natsagiin Bagabandi]], who received 59% of the vote. Voter turnout was 83%.<ref>Nohlen ''et al''., p491</ref>

